From 4c2c644cbe736676ad68d958da59b9c30e7fb820 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ohgur <ohgur@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 00:28:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hipGraph: propagate UpdateAQLPacket failure out of
 hipGraphExecUpdate

hipGraphExecUpdate assigns the result of GraphExecBase::UpdateAQLPacket to
status and then never inspects it. When the recapture fails, for example when
a kernarg allocation cannot be satisfied under device-memory exhaustion, the
function falls through to updateResult_out = hipGraphExecUpdateSuccess and
returns hipSuccess while the executable graph still holds the PREVIOUSLY
captured packet. The next launch replays that stale packet: the kernel runs
with the old arguments, which is silent wrong output, and once the kernarg pool
recycles the slot the packet itself can be malformed.

Every other UpdateAQLPacket call site in this file already propagates the
status via HIP_RETURN(status); this one is the outlier. Surface the failure the
same way, reporting the offending node in hErrorNode_out and
hipGraphExecUpdateError in updateResult_out so callers can fall back to
destroying and reinstantiating the exec.

Reproduced on gfx1100 (Radeon RX 7900 XTX) with a reproducer that exhausts
device memory and then repeatedly updates and relaunches a captured
single-node graph, checking the value the kernel actually wrote:

  stock                        SIGSEGV inside libamdhip64
  with the kernarg null checks kernel wrote 83106 when it asked for 83107
  with this change             clean hipErrorGraphExecUpdateFailure

Verified present at develop as of this base commit.
---
 projects/clr/hipamd/src/hip_graph.cpp | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/projects/clr/hipamd/src/hip_graph.cpp b/projects/clr/hipamd/src/hip_graph.cpp
index 7bbf2df9d2..59bf6f05f8 100644
--- a/projects/clr/hipamd/src/hip_graph.cpp
+++ b/projects/clr/hipamd/src/hip_graph.cpp
@@ -2830,6 +2830,16 @@ hipError_t hipGraphExecUpdate(hipGraphExec_t hGraphExec, hipGraph_t hGraph,
         auto graphExec = reinterpret_cast<hip::GraphExecBase*>(hGraphExec);
         if (newGraphNodes[i]->GraphCaptureEnabled()) {
           status = graphExec->UpdateAQLPacket(reinterpret_cast<hip::GraphKernelNode*>(oldGraphExecNodes[i]));
+          if (status != hipSuccess) {
+            // A packet recapture failure (e.g. kernarg allocation under device-memory
+            // exhaustion) leaves the exec holding the PREVIOUSLY captured packet.  Reporting
+            // success here makes the next launch execute that stale packet: silent output
+            // corruption, and with kernarg-pool recycling a malformed AQL packet.  Surface it,
+            // as every other UpdateAQLPacket call site in this file already does.
+            *hErrorNode_out = reinterpret_cast<hipGraphNode_t>(newGraphNodes[i]);
+            *updateResult_out = hipGraphExecUpdateError;
+            HIP_RETURN(hipErrorGraphExecUpdateFailure);
+          }
         }
       }
     } else {

